{% schema %}
  {
    
    "name": "Section 2",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-538131296174474026 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/e49d78-3/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=538131296040256298&sectionId=538131296174474026)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrpx59fHRV_text","label":"ggrpx59fHRV_text","default":"Dad Bod Chronicles: How to Lose the Love Handles While Raising the Little Ones"},{"type":"html","id":"ggX2ilwSika_text","label":"ggX2ilwSika_text","default":"<p>Fatherhood brings immense joy, but also lifestyle changes that can impact fitness. Many dads struggle with stubborn belly fat due to hormonal changes, increased stress, less sleep, and limited time for fitness. This guide covers practical strategies for dads to target and lose belly fat without sacrificing quality time with family.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg9GIF23N0s_text","label":"gg9GIF23N0s_text","default":"Why the Dad Bod Happens (and Why It’s So Hard to Get Rid Of)"},{"type":"html","id":"ggaVX7fBRvK_text","label":"ggaVX7fBRvK_text","default":"<p>Source: Freepik</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggTZoRWVkfF_text","label":"ggTZoRWVkfF_text","default":"<p>Ah, the dad bod—both a badge of honor and a challenging side effect of fatherhood. With responsibilities piling up, many dads find themselves facing physical changes that weren’t part of the plan. Let’s break down why this extra padding around the midsection seems so determined to stick around.</p><p>=&gt; Find more about Dad Bod Biology<span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"> </span><a href=\"https://wellnessnest.co/blogs/news/the-dad-bod-explained\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><strong><u>Here</u></strong></span></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Energy Expenditure Hits the Brakes</strong></span></p><p>As you transition into fatherhood, especially in your 30s, you might notice weight gain and changes in body composition. Your daily energy expenditure often drops due to lifestyle changes: less physical activity, more sitting time, and gradual muscle loss from reduced activity. Since<a href=\"https://www.mayoclinic.org/healthy-lifestyle/weight-loss/in-depth/metabolism/art-20046508\"> <span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>muscle burns more calories than fat</u></span></a>, this combination of factors makes weight gain more likely, especially around the belly. The good news? These changes are primarily lifestyle-related, meaning they can be countered with regular movement and strength training, even with a busy schedule.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Stress and Sleep: The Dynamic Duo</strong></span></p><p>Fatherhood can be a rewarding experience, but it also comes with plenty of stress and sleepless nights. When you’re stressed or sleep-deprived, your body produces more<span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"> </span><a href=\"https://www.todaysdietitian.com/newarchives/111609p38.shtml\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>cortisol</u></span></a>, the “stress hormone.” High cortisol levels are associated with increased appetite, cravings for high-calorie foods, and, you guess, belly fat storage. Plus, lack of sleep messes with hormones like <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17212793/\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>leptin and ghrelin</u></span></a> that help control hunger and fullness, making it harder to stick to healthier choices.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Hormones and Aging</strong></span></p><p>Testosterone plays a major role in <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2917954/\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>muscle maintenance</u></span></a> and fat distribution, but as we age, testosterone levels naturally decline. Lower testosterone can mean less muscle and more fat accumulation, especially around the midsection. And muscle burns more calories than fat, so when muscle mass drops, your calorie-burning potential dips right along with it, adding to the challenge.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Time - Or Lack Thereof</strong></span></p><p>Between work, family, and trying to find a few minutes for yourself, exercise often takes a backseat. And without consistency, fat loss becomes a lot harder. But the good news is that with a few creative solutions, you can fit in movement without missing out on family time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, what’s the solution? It’s all about getting creative, which brings us to the next step:</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gggk43ll1fS_text","label":"gggk43ll1fS_text","default":"<strong>Kid-Friendly Cardio: Get Moving While Spending Time with the Little Ones</strong>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggaujKeIn_v_text","label":"ggaujKeIn_v_text","default":"<p>Source: Freepik</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggxD5F8ssSO_text","label":"ggxD5F8ssSO_text","default":"<p>Who says working out has to mean gym memberships and solo sweat sessions? As a dad, you’ve got the best workout partners right in front of you - your kids! From chasing them around the yard to playing games that sneak in cardio, there are countless ways to burn calories without missing out on family time. Here are some kid-friendly cardio ideas that don’t feel like workouts but will keep that heart pumping and the belly fat at bay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>The Classic Chase Game</strong></span></p><p>Nothing gets your heart rate up faster than a good old game of “Chase the Dad.” Kids love it, and all that sprinting, dodging, and laughing adds up to a solid cardio session. You’ll be amazed at how many calories you can burn while playing tag, hide-and-seek, or “monster chase.” Plus, it’s a great way to bond and share a lot of laughs along the way.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Obstacle Course Olympics</strong></span></p><p>Transform your backyard (or living room) into a mini obstacle course using pillows, chairs, and jump ropes. Set up stations for activities like jumping jacks, crawling under tables, and racing around cones. Not only will you get your heart rate up, but your kids will get an outlet for their boundless energy. You’ll both be panting by the end, and it’ll feel more like an adventure than a workout.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Dance Parties Anytime, Anywhere</strong></span></p><p>If there’s one thing kids love, it’s moving to a beat. Crank up some tunes and let loose in the living room with a family dance-off. Pick songs with an upbeat tempo, and throw in some moves that make you jump, twist, and move those arms. It’s great cardio, a core workout, and maybe even a fun family tradition in the making. Bonus: This one works as well on rainy days as it does in the backyard.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Biking, Scooting, or Hiking Adventures</strong></span></p><p>Got a bike, scooter, or pair of running shoes? Gather the family for a biking or hiking adventure. Opt for a nearby park or trail, pack some snacks, and make a day of it. You can keep up a good pace while the kids race ahead or take turns “leading the pack.” Hills are your friend here - they’ll get your quads and glutes working hard, and the kids will get a thrill from tackling them together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Sports Drills and Backyard Games</strong></span></p><p>Whether it’s soccer, basketball, or throwing a frisbee, engaging in sports drills with your kids is a surefire way to get your heart racing. Try simple drills like dribbling, sprinting, or “around the world” shots. You’ll be active, and your little ones will start picking up skills (or, let’s be honest, probably just giggle a lot watching you try to keep up).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Spending time with the kids while staying active doesn’t just improve physical health; it also creates cherished memories. By the end of the day, you’ll both feel accomplished, connected, and, hopefully, just tired enough for a good night’s sleep.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIMycOvou4_text","label":"ggIMycOvou4_text","default":"<strong>Stress, Sleep, and the Snack Attack: Beating the Fatherhood Fat Traps</strong>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggnC9Z88pHb_text","label":"ggnC9Z88pHb_text","default":"<p>Source: Freepik</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggFJeTDTG7k_text","label":"ggFJeTDTG7k_text","default":"<p>Fatherhood brings a world of joy, but let’s face it: it also brings stress, sleepless nights, and plenty of snack-time temptations. These three “fat traps” are notorious for sabotaging the best fitness intentions, especially when it comes to that stubborn belly area.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Stress: The Silent Belly-Fat Culprit</strong></span></p><p>Raising kids is one of life’s greatest adventures, but it’s no secret that it’s also one of the most stressful. Whether it’s running to soccer practices or getting the kids to bed on time, stress sneaks in and impacts your body in ways you might not expect. Stress triggers the release of <strong>cortisol</strong>, the “stress hormone” linked to belly fat retention. Elevated cortisol levels signal your body to store more fat—especially around the midsection—making it tough to trim down.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Turkesterone Advanced Formula</strong> includes <a href=\"https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/#:~:text=Overall%2C%20the%20studies%20found%20that,)%20levels%2C%20compared%20with%20placebo.\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>Ashwagandha</u></span></a>, a powerful adaptogen well-known for reducing cortisol levels and helping the body handle stress more effectively. Incorporating this supplement can support a balanced stress response, giving you a better shot at fighting fat storage caused by stress.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:20px;\"><strong>Sleep (or the Lack Thereof)</strong></span></p><p>Ask any dad: sleep becomes a luxury after kids come into the picture. But consistently missing out on quality sleep impacts more than just your mood and energy levels—it also messes with hunger hormones. Lack of sleep raises ghrelin (the hunger hormone) and lowers leptin (the hormone that signals fullness), creating a perfect recipe for overeating. Poor sleep also increases cravings for high-calorie, quick-fix foods, which tend to land around the belly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here, <strong>Turkesterone Advanced Formula</strong> shines again. With ingredients like <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/sleepadvances/article/5/1/zpae047/7710213\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>Tongkat Ali</u></span></a><strong>,</strong> a natural remedy that supports energy and hormone balance - this formula can be a game-changer for dads looking to combat sleep-related weight gain. By supporting hormonal health, it can help you handle those sleepless nights a bit more gracefully.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>The Snack Attack: A Dad Bod’s Best Friend (and Worst Enemy)</strong></span></p><p>Snacks seem to appear out of nowhere when you have kids around, whether it’s leftover pizza crusts, half-eaten PB&amp;Js, or goldfish crackers, and family time BBQ. Combine that with limited time for sit-down meals, and snacking becomes a near-daily event. The issue? These quick bites add up, and they often lead to extra calories that love to settle right in the belly area.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Research suggests that Tongkat Ali can <a href=\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Changes-in-Leptin-in-Relation-to-Increased-Levels-Faisal-Haque/221264fe6b38a98d853bac24a4a67099d6ef1fd2#:~:text=Eurycoma%20Longifolia%20root%20extract%20can%20significantly%20decrease,the%20possibility%20of%20decreased%20body%20fat%20content.\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><u>decrease leptin levels in the blood</u></span></a>, a hormone responsible for regulating hunger and fat storage. Lower leptin levels are often associated with decreased appetite and reduced body fat, as the body starts to use stored fat more effectively. By helping to decrease leptin, Tongkat Ali may support natural weight management and a reduction in body fat content.</p><p>=&gt; Find how to change from <a href=\"https://wellnessnest.co/blogs/news/dad-bod-to-rad-bod\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;\"><strong><u>Dad Bod to Rad bod</u></strong></span></a></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggnxZ6NiIAE_text","label":"ggnxZ6NiIAE_text","default":"<strong>Progress, Not Perfection: Celebrating Small Wins on the Dad Bod Journey</strong>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg-71aRsR4S_text","label":"gg-71aRsR4S_text","default":"<p>Let’s face it: getting fit as a dad is a marathon, not a sprint. Between work, family responsibilities, and, well, life, the perfect routine rarely exists. But here’s the great news: you don’t need perfection to see progress. Embracing small wins and celebrating every step forward can keep you motivated, prevent burnout, and make your fitness journey a sustainable one.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Set Realistic, Bite-Sized Goals</strong></span></p><p>When starting out, it’s tempting to aim for an all-or-nothing transformation. But focusing on smaller, achievable goals—like taking a 15-minute walk daily or cutting out that extra soda—sets you up for real, lasting success. Each tiny improvement brings you one step closer to your big-picture goals and builds confidence along the way. Remember, <strong>small wins build momentum</strong> and create the foundation for more significant changes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Track Progress </strong></span><a href=\"https://www.today.com/health/diet-fitness/non-scale-victories-nsv-rcna98828\"><span style=\"color:#0037FF;font-size:19px;\"><strong><u>Beyond the Scale</u></strong></span></a></p><p>It’s easy to get discouraged when the scale doesn’t budge. But your journey is about much more than numbers. Consider other measures of success that reflect your progress, like feeling more energetic, lifting heavier weights, or fitting more comfortably into your favorite jeans. Notice and appreciate these “non-scale victories.” Celebrating improvements in strength, stamina, and even daily mood can make the journey feel rewarding - even when the scale is stubborn.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Celebrate Every Win (No Matter How Small)</strong></span></p><p>Did you skip the sugary snack today? Choose water over soda? Squeeze in a quick workout? These may seem minor, but they’re wins worth celebrating! Every good choice is a building block that reinforces healthy habits and brings you closer to your goal. Treat yourself to a little reward—like a family outing or a new fitness gadget, to mark these moments. Acknowledging small successes keeps you motivated and reminds you that progress is happening.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Find Support (And Share Your Wins!)</strong></span></p><p>A great way to stay motivated is to involve others in your journey. Share your milestones with friends, family, or a community of fellow dads with similar goals. A quick update or photo of your progress keeps you accountable and lets you celebrate your success with people who understand your challenges. You may even inspire someone else to start their own journey. Plus, having a support system makes the journey less lonely - and a lot more fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Practice Self-Compassion</strong></span></p><p>Slip-ups are part of the process. Skipped a workout? Ate too many snacks at movie night? It’s okay. Progress is about persistence, not perfection. The key is to recognize that slip-ups happen and to pick up where you left off without guilt. Remember, fitness is a lifestyle, and one missed workout or a splurge meal doesn’t undo your hard work. Embracing a forgiving mindset helps you stay consistent in the long run.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><strong>Progress Over Perfection</strong></span></p><p>Each choice, no matter how small, brings you closer to the stronger, healthier version of yourself. Remember, this journey is about progress, not a race to perfection. So, give yourself credit for every effort, big or small, and enjoy the process. You’re not just working toward a goal; you’re setting an example for your kids on the power of persistence and self-care.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now go ahead and celebrate those wins - they’re the fuel that will keep you going!</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg6X30OJCMD_text","label":"gg6X30OJCMD_text","default":"Turkesterone Advanced Formula"},{"type":"html","id":"ggb7kEWmUtI_text","label":"ggb7kEWmUtI_text","default":"<p>Find your younger self again!</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA8AZcCeik_label","label":"ggA8AZcCeik_label","default":"Shop now"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA8AZcCeik_outOfStockLabel","label":"ggA8AZcCeik_outOfStockLabel","default":"Out of stock"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA8AZcCeik_unavailableLabel","label":"ggA8AZcCeik_unavailableLabel","default":"Unavailable"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYxE_gWaDi_text","label":"ggYxE_gWaDi_text","default":"<p><a href=\"https://wellnessnest.co/products/turkesterone-advanced-formula\"><u>Learn more</u></a></p>"}],
